## PCB sample: simple rectangular conductor in an air box
##
## Required labels:
##   block 1 = "conductor"  (the copper trace, 10mm x 1mm x 0.035mm)
##   block 2 = "air"        (the surrounding air box)
##
## Note: PCB analysis primarily uses FastHenry .inp; this .jou creates a
##       minimal mesh for field evaluation in NGSolve.
##
## Build policy:
##   - SUBTRACT conductor from air with `keep_tool` (otherwise conductor
##     volume disappears and `block 1 add volume 1` errors out)
##   - imprint+merge on the resulting volumes shares the conductor-air
##     interface (Consolidated N pair of surfaces, N > 0)

reset

# === 1. Conductor (vol 1): 10 mm x 1 mm x 0.035 mm copper trace ===
brick x 0.010 y 0.001 z 0.000035
move volume 1 x 0.005 y 0.0005 z 0.0000175

# === 2. Air box (vol 2) enclosing the conductor ===
brick x 0.020 y 0.010 z 0.005
move volume 2 x 0.010 y 0.005 z 0.0025

# === 3. Carve a conductor cavity in the air, KEEPING the conductor ===
# `keep_tool` is required so that block 1 still has volume 1 to add.
subtract volume 1 from volume 2 keep_tool

# === 4. Imprint + merge: shares the conductor-air interface ===
imprint volume 1 2
merge volume 1 2

# === 5. Mesh ===
volume 1 scheme tetmesh
volume 1 size 0.0005
mesh volume 1

volume 2 scheme tetmesh
volume 2 size 0.002
mesh volume 2

# === 6. Blocks ===
block 1 add volume 1
block 1 name "conductor"
block 2 add volume 2
block 2 name "air"
